LANGUAGE RULES
- Swift only unless explicitly requested otherwise
- Use modern Swift (async/await)
- No legacy Objective-C patterns
- No UIKit

ARCHITECTURE RULES
- Feature-based folder structure
- One primary type per file
- File size must stay under 300 lines
- Internal access by default
- Public only when required for API surface
- No global mutable state

SWIFT RULES
- Prefer structs over classes
- Use final classes when reference semantics are required
- No singletons unless unavoidable
- No force unwraps
- No implicitly unwrapped optionals
- Prefer immutability
- Explicit error handling
- Avoid Any
- Avoid magic numbers

SWIFTUI RULES
- Views must be stateless
- Business logic must live in ViewModels
- Use @State only for local view state
- Use @StateObject for owned ViewModels
- Use @ObservedObject for injected ViewModels
- Avoid @EnvironmentObject unless globally justified
- No side effects in view bodies
- No networking inside views

CONCURRENCY RULES
- Prefer async/await
- Use Task over DispatchQueue
- MainActor for UI mutations
- No blocking calls on main thread
- Cancellation must be respected

APPKIT INTEROP RULES
- Use NSViewRepresentable / NSWindowRepresentable
- No direct AppKit logic in SwiftUI views
- Keep AppKit isolated and minimal

ERROR HANDLING
- Use typed errors
- No silent failures
- No empty catch blocks

PERFORMANCE RULES
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders
- Avoid heavy work in init
- Memoize expensive computations when needed

DEFAULT BEHAVIOR
- When asked for help, respond with corrected or improved code only
- When asked to debug, return the fixed code
- When asked to refactor, return the refactored code
- Never explain changes unless explicitly requested
